<InfoLayout title="About Auspicious Music" description="The purpose, scope and ownership of this independent music-technology publication." canonicalPath="/about/" lede="A small, independent publication about the point where musical decisions become files, recordings, instruments and deliverables.">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0">What this site is for</h2>
  <p>Auspicious Music publishes practical guides for music production, Ableton Live, acoustic recording, sampling and music used in films or live events. The common thread is not a genre or a list of products. It is the handoff between an intention and a system another person can understand.</p>
  <p>The first editorial release is intentionally narrow: eight substantial guides rather than dozens of empty topic pages. New pages are added only when they answer a real decision and can state how their claims were produced.</p>

  <h2>Who publishes it</h2>
  <p>The current publisher is <a href="/authors/">Matthias Ramahi</a>, based in Erkrath, Germany. He owns and maintains the site, commissions or writes its editorial work and is responsible for corrections. Contact and statutory details are published under <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> and <a href="/legal/">Impressum</a>.</p>

  <h2>What “independent” means here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No former owner, author or product is represented as part of the new publication.</li>
    <li>No review verdict is published without a documented test.</li>
    <li>Source-based guides are labelled as source-based.</li>
    <li>Commercial or project relationships relevant to a link are disclosed on the page.</li>
    <li>The site currently carries no display advertising or affiliate tracking.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The relationship to the former website</h2>
  <p>The domain previously hosted a different music-technology site. Domain ownership does not transfer authorship or rights in its former text, files, images or software. The <a href="/about/history-and-relaunch/">history and relaunch note</a> explains which old addresses are documented, which material is not republished and why unrelated spam URLs are not redirected into the new site.</p>

  <h2>Related projects</h2>
  <p>Some guides may point to a real project in the publisher’s portfolio when it materially helps the reader. For example, the wedding-planning guide links to the separate performance website of violist Kim Marie Borger. That relationship is disclosed in the article; the link carries no affiliate fee and is not presented as an independent endorsement.</p>

  <div class="note"><p><strong>Indexing safeguard</strong>Preview deployments are blocked from search indexing by default. The production build becomes indexable only through an explicit environment setting after domain, legal, redirect and crawl checks have passed.</p></div>
</InfoLayout>
